 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes its veterinarian directory the other way round: every specialty it knows, each with the veterinarians who hold it `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each specialty appears under the name the clinic stores for it. Each veterinarian appears by full name, first name then last name. The page lists specialties rather than the whole roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it. Every specialty appears on a single page. The page is read-only. It is reached by its address alone, and no other page links to it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name on a single page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty held by veterinarians, when the specialty directory is opened, then each of them is listed under it by first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given any other page of the system, when it is rendered, then it carries no link to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A veterinarian holding several specialties appears under each of them.
+2. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian under it.
+3. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+4. A specialty's name is shown as stored in every language; only the page's own wording follows the reader's language.
+5. The page offers no way to add, change, or remove a veterinarian or a specialty, as NG-2 records.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
